output:
I've written the signal engine, but I haven't run it. The directory was empty, so I built it from scratch, and I couldn't syntax-check it because the check was blocked. Apps Script can only run inside Google, so your first run in the editor is the real test.

The files are `Code.gs` and `appsscript.json`, both in `<workdir>`.

## What it does

- Every morning at 7:00 (London time) it collects threads labelled **Signals** that it hasn't digested before.
- It scores each thread against two keyword lists, **Lease law** and **Council planning**, and counts a subject match three times as heavily as a body match.
- It emails you a single digest. High-scoring items come first in each section, with sender, a snippet and a link. Anything scoring below 3 goes under "Everything else" as a one-line list.
- It then tags the threads it sent with a label called `Signals-Digested`, so nothing appears twice. The tagging happens only after the email goes out, so a failed run is retried the next day.
- On a day with nothing new, it sends no email.

## Setup

1. Go to **script.google.com**, choose **New project**, and name it "Signal Engine".
2. Paste the contents of `Code.gs` over the default `Code.gs` file.
3. Open **Project Settings** (the cog) and tick **Show "appsscript.json" manifest file in editor**. Go back to the editor, open `appsscript.json` and paste in my version. It sets the London timezone and keeps the permissions narrow: read and label Gmail, send mail, and manage its own trigger.
4. Choose `previewDigest` in the function dropdown and press **Run**. Google will ask you to authorise the script. You may need to click "Advanced" and then "Go to Signal Engine (unsafe)", which is normal for your own scripts. The digest appears in the execution log and nothing is sent or labelled, so you can check it safely.
5. Run `setup` once. This creates the `Signals-Digested` label and the daily 7am trigger.
6. Run `sendDailyDigest` once by hand to get your first real digest.

## Tuning

- Your first digest will cover the whole backlog, up to 200 threads. If that's too noisy, apply `Signals-Digested` to old threads in Gmail first, or lower `MAX_THREADS`.
- The keyword lists are my guess at UK terms (Renters' Rights, Section 21, Article 4, HMO and so on). Edit `CONFIG.TOPICS` to match what you actually get. A few words are broad, such as `council`, `regulation` and `legislation`. If they pull in noise, remove them or raise `MIN_SCORE`.
- If a newsletter lands in the wrong section, check whether its subject or body hits the other list more heavily.
- The digest picks the best-scoring topic for each thread, so a thread never appears in both sections.

## Limitations

- A thread already digested won't come back if someone replies to it later.
- Scoring is plain keyword matching with no understanding of context.
- Gmail caps scripts at roughly 20 to 30 minutes of run time a day. 40 threads a day is far below that.

I haven't committed anything. Tell me if you'd like it committed, or if you'd like the keywords tuned after you've seen the first preview.
--- appsscript.json ---
{
  "timeZone": "Europe/London",
  "exceptionLogging": "STACKDRIVER",
  "runtimeVersion": "V8",
  "oauthScopes": [
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify",
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/script.send_mail",
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/script.scriptapp"
  ]
}

--- Code.gs ---
/**
 * Harbourside Lettings - signal engine.
 * Reads undigested threads under the Gmail label "Signals", scores them against
 * topic keywords, and emails one daily digest to the script owner.
 */

const CONFIG = {
  LABEL: 'Signals',
  DONE_LABEL: 'Signals-Digested', // top-level on purpose: label:Signals also matches nested "Signals/..." labels
  MAX_THREADS: 200,
  SEND_HOUR: 7, // local hour (per appsscript.json timeZone) the digest is sent
  MIN_SCORE: 3, // below this, a thread is listed under "Everything else"
  SUBJECT_WEIGHT: 3,
  BODY_WEIGHT: 1,
  BODY_CHARS: 3000,
  TOPICS: {
    'Lease law': [
      'renters\' rights', 'section 21', 'section 8', 'possession', 'tenancy', 'assured shorthold',
      'periodic tenancy', 'tenancy deposit', 'deposit protection', 'eviction', 'landlord and tenant',
      'leasehold', 'ground rent', 'lease extension', 'right to manage', 'epc', 'minimum energy',
      'selective licensing', 'hmo licen', 'gas safety', 'electrical safety', 'awaab', 'decent homes',
      'tribunal', 'rent increase', 'section 13', 'legislation', 'regulation', 'consultation response'
    ],
    'Council planning': [
      'planning application', 'planning notice', 'planning permission', 'planning committee',
      'change of use', 'article 4', 'hmo', 'local plan', 'development control', 'site notice',
      'neighbour notification', 'listed building', 'conservation area', 'permitted development',
      'section 106', 'cil', 'planning appeal', 'licensing notice', 'council'
    ]
  }
};

/** Run once by hand: authorises the script and creates the daily trigger. */
function setup() {
  getOrCreateLabel_(CONFIG.DONE_LABEL);
  installTrigger();
  Logger.log('Setup done. Run previewDigest() to see what the first digest would contain.');
}

function installTrigger() {
  ScriptApp.getProjectTriggers()
    .filter(t => t.getHandlerFunction() === 'sendDailyDigest')
    .forEach(t => ScriptApp.deleteTrigger(t));
  ScriptApp.newTrigger('sendDailyDigest').timeBased().everyDays(1).atHour(CONFIG.SEND_HOUR).create();
}

/** Logs the digest without sending it or labelling anything. */
function previewDigest() {
  const digest = buildDigest_();
  Logger.log(digest ? digest.text : 'Nothing new under "' + CONFIG.LABEL + '".');
}

function sendDailyDigest() {
  const digest = buildDigest_();
  if (!digest) return; // nothing new: no email
  const me = Session.getEffectiveUser().getEmail();
  MailApp.sendEmail({
    to: me,
    subject: 'Signals digest: ' + digest.summary,
    body: digest.text,
    htmlBody: digest.html
  });
  const done = getOrCreateLabel_(CONFIG.DONE_LABEL);
  // Labels are applied only after the email is sent, so a failed run is retried, not lost.
  for (let i = 0; i < digest.threads.length; i += 100) {
    done.addToThreads(digest.threads.slice(i, i + 100));
  }
}

function buildDigest_() {
  const query = 'label:' + CONFIG.LABEL + ' -label:' + CONFIG.DONE_LABEL;
  const threads = GmailApp.search(query, 0, CONFIG.MAX_THREADS);
  if (!threads.length) return null;

  const buckets = {};
  Object.keys(CONFIG.TOPICS).forEach(t => buckets[t] = []);
  const other = [];

  threads.forEach(thread => {
    const msg = thread.getMessages()[thread.getMessageCount() - 1];
    const subject = thread.getFirstMessageSubject();
    const body = msg.getPlainBody().slice(0, CONFIG.BODY_CHARS);
    const item = {
      subject: subject,
      from: msg.getFrom().replace(/<.*>/, '').replace(/"/g, '').trim() || msg.getFrom(),
      url: thread.getPermalink(),
      snippet: body.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim().slice(0, 220),
      score: 0
    };
    let bestTopic = null;
    Object.keys(CONFIG.TOPICS).forEach(topic => {
      const s = score_(CONFIG.TOPICS[topic], subject, body);
      if (s > item.score) { item.score = s; bestTopic = topic; }
    });
    if (bestTopic && item.score >= CONFIG.MIN_SCORE) buckets[bestTopic].push(item);
    else other.push(item);
  });

  const sortDesc = (a, b) => b.score - a.score;
  const sections = Object.keys(buckets).map(t => ({ title: t, items: buckets[t].sort(sortDesc), detail: true }));
  sections.push({ title: 'Everything else', items: other, detail: false });

  const counts = Object.keys(buckets).map(t => buckets[t].length + ' ' + t.toLowerCase()).join(', ');
  return {
    threads: threads,
    summary: counts + ', ' + other.length + ' other',
    text: renderText_(sections),
    html: renderHtml_(sections)
  };
}

function score_(keywords, subject, body) {
  const subj = subject.toLowerCase();
  const text = body.toLowerCase();
  let total = 0;
  keywords.forEach(k => {
    const kw = k.toLowerCase();
    if (subj.indexOf(kw) !== -1) total += CONFIG.SUBJECT_WEIGHT;
    if (text.indexOf(kw) !== -1) total += CONFIG.BODY_WEIGHT;
  });
  return total;
}

function renderText_(sections) {
  return sections.filter(s => s.items.length).map(s => {
    const lines = s.items.map(i => s.detail
      ? '- ' + i.subject + ' (' + i.from + ')\n  ' + i.snippet + '\n  ' + i.url
      : '- ' + i.subject + ' (' + i.from + ')');
    return s.title.toUpperCase() + ' (' + s.items.length + ')\n' + lines.join('\n');
  }).join('\n\n');
}

function renderHtml_(sections) {
  const esc = s => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  const body = sections.filter(s => s.items.length).map(s => {
    const lis = s.items.map(i => s.detail
      ? '<li style="margin-bottom:10px"><a href="' + esc(i.url) + '"><b>' + esc(i.subject) + '</b></a>' +
        '<br><span style="color:#666">' + esc(i.from) + '</span><br>' + esc(i.snippet) + '</li>'
      : '<li><a href="' + esc(i.url) + '">' + esc(i.subject) + '</a> <span style="color:#666">- ' + esc(i.from) + '</span></li>');
    return '<h3>' + esc(s.title) + ' (' + s.items.length + ')</h3><ul>' + lis.join('') + '</ul>';
  }).join('');
  return '<div style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px">' + body + '</div>';
}

function getOrCreateLabel_(name) {
  return GmailApp.getUserLabelByName(name) || GmailApp.createLabel(name);
}
